                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                        "entry_id": "d1af7165-214b-3ebd-9727-9fbedafa9cec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Uncool, unfashionable, but comfortably so."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1ff44ad-1409-4b8c-9089-212256cccfd2",
                                "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                                "text": "\"But I remember everything about that day. What everyone was wearing, all the daggy things people said in the car on the way into town. The smell of stubble, upholstery. The taste of tomato in my throat from lunch.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dcda339c-76c8-4540-b196-ae5fd6e70e17",
                                "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                                "text": "We wore hippie clothes, looking more daggy than cool."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db7e888b-169d-4fbf-bdc8-252b258fc786",
                                "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                                "text": "I began to feel even more daggy when Bianca swanned me around to meet her sexy, skinny and beautiful friends."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68b211a3-b11e-452a-956e-f34dbf912193",
                                "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                                "text": "The daggiest house in the Bay, that was how people talked about the Isherwood House."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04f6d776-e2ea-4d44-bf23-6f8d386a41ac",
                                "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                                "text": "Actually this wasn′t too bad as a jazz venue, being in the daggiest pub in the daggiest part of Capalaba which, in 2004 was still a pretty daggy suburb."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26f4fe20-c0af-430c-9dd4-77e157068262",
                                "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                                "text": "“Yeah, I know, I-I was starting to like her too, even though she said I dress \"daggy,\" whatever that means.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d280e3f9-62f2-417a-bfff-2f46dc57664c",
                                "sense_id": "6b5a719d-f048-3ee0-be56-3dda9dd9e6e5",
                                "text": "In a daggy Canadian nightclub, Clark Kent lookalike Clif asked Pilar Mitchell for a dance – and her life changed[.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
